{SECT 0 {EXCHG {PARA 18 "" 0 "" {TEXT 286 15 "Assignment Five" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 215 11 " Problem 1." }{TEXT 287 3 "   " }
}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 287 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 287 44 "Genera
te 8 random 3 by 3 matrices using the " }{TEXT 216 12 "RandomMatrix" }
{TEXT 287 19 " command from the  " }{TEXT 217 13 "LinearAlgebra" }
{TEXT 287 42 " package. As each matrix is generated use " }{TEXT 218 
11 "Eigenvalues" }{TEXT 287 160 " to compute its eigenvalues. Then tak
e the product of the eigenvalues, and check that for each matrix, this
 product is equal to the determinant of the matrix.  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 
"" {TEXT 287 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 287 1 "[" }{TEXT 219 6 "Hint
: " }{TEXT 287 79 "The product will be complicated algebraically and y
ou will need to apply first " }{TEXT 220 6 "expand" }{TEXT 287 7 ", th
en " }{TEXT 221 8 "simplify" }{TEXT 287 132 " to reduce the product of
 the eigenvalues to an integer. First try to do for a single matrix , \+
then make a loop to do it 8 times.]  " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "restart:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 20 
